:0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"Following the postgresql examples of the usage of enums that are in the docs https://docs.sqlalchemy.org/en/14/dialects/postgresql.html#sqlalchemy.dialects.postgresql.ENUM:\r\n\r\n```python\r\nfrom sqlalchemy import Column, Integer, MetaData\r\nfrom sqlalchemy.orm import declarative_base\r\nfrom sqlalchemy.dialects.postgresql import ENUM\r\n\r\nmetadata = MetaData(schema=\"other\")\r\nBase = declarative_base(metadata=metadata)\r\n\r\nclass T1(Base):\r\n    __tablename__ = \"t1\"\r\n\r\n    id = Column(Integer, primary_key=True)\r\n    enumerator = Column(ENUM('a', 'b', 'c', name='myenum', metadata=metadata))\r\n\r\nBase.metadata.create_all()\r\n```\r\n\r\nWhat I expect is a new table created in the schema other and a new data type created in the schema other.\r\nHowever, the enum is always created in the schema public... Am I missing something or this is an expected behaviour?\r\n\r\n**Versions**\r\n - OS: Windows 10\r\n - Python: 3.8\r\n - SQLAlchemy: 1.4.11\r\n - Database: Postgresql 13\r\n\r\n\r\nThanks in advance","closed_by":{"login":"sqlalchemy-bot","id":36047385,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MDQ3Mzg1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36047385?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot","html_url":"https://github.com/sqlalchemy-bot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/us